cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RSAS in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "RSAS: RNA Structure Analysis Suite"
abstract: >-
  Functional RNAs regulate cellular processes through dynamic structures governed by folding thermodynamics.
  We developed RNA Structure Analysis Suite (RSAS), a modular computational platform for identifying, scoring, 
  and characterizing RNA secondary structures across sequence datasets. RSAS comprises original modules for thermodynamic analysis,
  candidate scoring, genome sequence extraction, motif accessibility, and synthetic RNA design. Its primary advance is the
  integration of these capabilities into a customizable batch analysis and scoring framework that transforms RNA folding predictions
  into class-specific, motif-guided, and user-weighted workflows. Using RNA thermometers as a benchmark, we derived scoring features
  from previously validated thermometers, prioritized candidates from an Escherichia coli 5′ UTR dataset and validated seven novel
  RNA thermometers. Additionally, RSAS identified candidate RNA thermometers in other genomic and metagenomic datasets, as well as
  candidate HIV-like ribosomal frameshifting elements in viral sequences. RSAS provides a customizable framework for discovering
  structured RNA regulatory elements across diverse sequence spaces and is available at https://github.com/RNAThermometer/RSAS.
type: software
authors:
  version: "4.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-03"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/RNAThermometer/RSAS"
url: "https://github.com/RNAThermometer/RSAS"
keywords:
